// allocation and no copy, so the bytes stay owned by the caller. (rt_cstr copies
// into a freshly packed NUL-terminated buffer and is used for process arguments.)
// C-layout field access for widths below one word. Portable byte-wise load/store so
// no target needs new instruction selection: `width` is 1, 2 or 4.
// C arrays inline in extern records (`f: [T; N]`) are copied whole into and out of Grail vectors.
// kind 0: integers and words (`size` bytes, sign-extended when `signed`); 1: f32 (binary32 in
